# MY School ERP — Project Context

Building a multi-tier school ERP for **MY School (myschools.pk)** on Frappe Framework + the open-source [Frappe Education](.cursor/rules/reference-frappe-education.mdc) app.

## Hierarchy (from the "Software Infrastructure" PDF)

Head Office (Chief Executive, Monitoring / Academic / Finance / Training / Admin Depts)
→ Cluster (Cluster Director, Academic Monitor, Audit Officer)
→ Branch (Director, Principal, Admin, Accountant, Teacher)
→ Campus (Junior / Kids / Senior, each with Incharge + Teachers / Admin)
→ Students → Parents (mobile/web portal).

## Unique ID format

- Student: `MYS-CL03-BR014-STU000245`
- Staff: `MYS-BR014-TCH0056`

## 22 modules required (per PDF)

Master Setup, Franchise Mgmt, SIS, HR/Staff, Campus Mgmt, Academic, Examination, Attendance, Finance/Fee, Parent Portal, Teacher Portal, Communication, Monitoring & Inspection, Transport, Library, LMS, Document Mgmt, Security/Role, Mobile App, Unique ID, Reporting.

## Why this scope

Frappe Education v16 ships with SIS, Fee, Class, Assessment, Student Portal — covers ~5 of 22 modules. The franchise hierarchy (Cluster/Branch/Campus multi-tenancy), custom ID system, monitoring/inspection workflows, parent mobile app, and several other modules are custom work on top.

## How to apply

- Treat the 22 modules as the scope ceiling.
- Build franchise hierarchy first — it's the foundation everything else scopes off of.
- Use ERPNext HR for staff, `frappe/lms` for LMS, custom DocTypes for what's missing.
- App lives at `frappe-bench/apps/myschools/`. Repo cwd is `/Users/ali/projects/myschools`.

